      <Comment source="PMN, zhang">Several unusual cofactors are involved in methanogenesis. One of those is |FRAME: CPD-7323|, a 2-hydroxyphenazine derivative which is linked via an ether bridge to a pentaisoprenoid side chain |CITS: [10941105]|. The reduced form of |FRAME: CPD-7323 Methanophenazine| serves as the electron donor for |FRAME: EC-1.8.98.1|.</Comment>
